### DevAssist Eval API — end-to-end request file (Task 8)
###
### Prerequisites:
###   - Ollama running locally with `nomic-embed-text` pulled (http://localhost:11434) —
###     the eval corpus is seeded at startup using Ollama embeddings, no Gemini key needed.
###   - GEMINI_API_KEY exported before starting the app IF you intend to exercise a request
###     that reaches the model — both the query-answering step inside
###     RagQueryService.answer(...) AND the LLM-as-judge scoring in JudgeService need it.
###     Without it, POST /api/eval/run still returns 200: RagExceptionHandler does NOT cover
###     this endpoint (EvalController is not in its assignableTypes list). Instead, each
###     question's underlying RagQueryService.answer(...) failure (e.g. a BeanCreationException
###     from the missing Gemini key) is caught per-question inside
###     EvaluationService.evaluateOne()'s own try/catch and recorded as that entry's
###     failureReason, and the run continues — you get a full 200 report where some or all
###     entries show a failure reason, not a 503.
###   - App started with `./mvnw spring-boot:run` (defaults to port 8080; adjust the
###     @baseUrl below if you run on a different port). No manual setup is required beyond
###     starting the app: EvalCorpusSeeder seeds the "RAG Evaluation Corpus" project and its
###     two documents (engineering-practices.txt, product-policy.txt) idempotently at startup.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080

### Run the evaluation
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/eval/run

> {%
    client.test("200 OK", () => response.status === 200);
    client.test("8 questions", () => response.body.results.length === 8);
    client.test("Has a pass/fail verdict", () => typeof response.body.summary.passed === "boolean");
%}

### Run it again - proves the ENDPOINT itself is repeatable and doesn't append
### duplicate results on repeated calls. This does NOT prove startup seeding is
### idempotent: EvalCorpusSeeder only runs once, at application boot, so this
### request never re-triggers it. Proving seeding idempotency would require
### restarting the app and re-checking that no duplicate documents were created.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/eval/run

> {%
    client.test("Still 8 questions, not 16", () => response.body.results.length === 8);
%}
